    why: "Identical buildings can carry very different income streams: one full of tenants paying above market with two years left, the other leased at market for ten. And a recorded price reflects the deal as well as the asset. Below-market debt that transfers with the property is worth real money, a seller under pressure accepts less and a buyer that needs to deploy capital pays more. That's why appraisers adjust comps for the rights sold, financing and conditions of sale before comparing buildings.",
