    why: "Pro rata value assumes you can realize your share of the whole, which a minority owner can't do alone. Its cash flow depends on decisions the controlling partner makes, and selling means finding a buyer willing to accept those terms, often the partner itself, which has little reason to pay full value. Control is worth something, so a controlling stake can even be worth a little more than pro rata. Discounts vary widely with the partnership agreement, so read it before applying a number.",
